course: dictionary
lesson: 9282
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «In old stories grown-ups spank children all the time» means to hit a child on the bottom with an open hand as a punishment. Today we know that hitting children is wrong.
explain: In the Just So Stories, Kipling uses spank in a silly way. The family «spanked him once more for luck», and the story is a joke, not a model for real life. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Context can also show a different, friendly meaning. «A spanking new bike» means a brand-new bike, and «at a spanking pace» means very fast. The words new and pace are the clues.
fact: Spank can be a verb, a noun or an adjective.
fact: «Spank» (verb) means to hit someone, usually a child, on the bottom with an open hand as a punishment.
fact: «A spank» (noun) means a slap on the bottom.
fact: Informal «spanking» means very good or fast, as in «a spanking new bike».
fact: In Scotland, Wales, Ireland, New Zealand and many other countries, it is against the law to hit children. You have a right not to be hit, and if someone hurts you, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «In old stories grown-ups spank children all the time.» What does spank mean here? | To kiss gently on the cheek | To run very fast | To sing a song to a baby | * To hit a child on the bottom with an open hand as a punishment
exercise: «The shop had a spanking new bike in the window.» What does spanking mean? | Broken | Very slow | Very old | * Brand-new
exercise: Your friend says a grown-up hurt her. What should she do? | Keep it secret forever | Hit back | Wait and say nothing | * Tell a trusted adult
test: «He ran off at a spanking pace.» What does spanking mean here? | Quiet | Very slow | * Very fast | Sleepy
test: In Scotland, hitting children is | A fun game for families | Allowed only on birthdays | Required by law at school | * Against the law
exam: In «a spank on the bottom», what is a spank? | A pair of trousers | A long, deep sleep | * A slap on the bottom | A type of fish
